<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 60 0 R/Alt(Block diagram of the Input Memory module. On the left, a bracket labeled AXIS input interface says that X, W, and B are on AXIS TDATA and that S, Q and new W are on AXIS TUSER. Along that label, there are four signals pointing into the module: AXIS_TDATA (WIDTH bits), AXIS_TUSER (S_BITS+8 bits), AXIS_TVALID, and AXIS_TREADY (pointing back out). Below that, reset and clk also point in. On the right, a bracket labeled interface to read data from the X memory groups X_read_addr (clog2(R*C) bits, pointing in) and X_data (WIDTH bits, pointing out); another bracket labeled interface to read data from the W memory groups W_read_addr (clog2(K*K) bits, pointing in) and W_data (WIDTH bits, pointing out). Also on the right, inputs_loaded points out and compute_finished points in; below those are S (S_BITS, pointing out), B (WIDTH, pointing out), and Q (7 bits, pointing out).)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block/BBox[72 87.692566 540 231.25781]>>]/K[103]/Pg 1002 0 R>>
